# Cross-link corpus groups — the crosslink gate scans each group INDEPENDENTLY.
#
# Format: a `[group-name]` header opens a group; following path lines (files or
# dirs) belong to it. '#' comments and blank lines are ignored. A file with no
# `[group]` header parses as a single group named `default` (legacy form).
#
# Each group is its own TF-IDF corpus: a cross-link candidate NEVER spans two
# groups. That is the point — it keeps unrelated surveys from proposing links at
# each other, while letting every corpus be checked on its own terms.
#
# Governs: .claude/hooks/validate-refs-on-dirty.sh (Stop-gate) and
# .githooks/pre-push. Severity toggle: .claude/crosslink-severity.
# To scope /cross-link to one group:
#     python viewer/tools/crosslink.py groups --group llm-methods
#
# Grouping is DATA-DRIVEN, not vibes: section-level TF-IDF + complete-linkage
# agglomeration (cut 0.20), satellites/wikis assigned by nearest-survey.
# Re-derive / audit after adding a survey:
#     python viewer/tools/crosslink-cluster.py propose
#     python viewer/tools/crosslink-cluster.py validate
# Never hand-expand this file with grep — use `crosslink.py groups` or --scope-file.

